// A client SYN with no TCP options gets a SYN-ACK carrying only MSS: Zhida echoes no
// window scale, SACK-permitted or timestamp option it was not offered. Zhida then sends
// to the client's default MSS, 536 (RFC 9293 3.7.1, no MSS option), and advertises its
// window unscaled. Linux behaves the same on all three.
// smoltcp 0.14.0 src/socket/tcp.rs; tap-echo, EchoServer and the turn order as in
// echo-and-close.pkt; TS and ISN conventions as in handshake-linux-options.pkt.
// - SYN-ACK <mss 1460> only: a SYN without the options leaves remote_win_scale None and
//   remote_has_sack false (1922-1923) and removes the TS generator (1929-1931), so the
//   SYN-ACK echoes neither (2610-2611) and carries no TS (2570-2573); MSS is always sent
//   (2777-2780). 24 header bytes, no EOL (src/wire/tcp.rs 998-1023, 1082-1084).
// - Window 48240 everywhere: without client wscale the shift is 0 (1925-1927). The SYN
//   has no MSS option, so the peer MSS 536 caps each of the 90 admitted frames
//   (128 KiB / 1460) at 536 bytes: 90 x 536 = 48240, under u16::MAX, sent unshifted from
//   the SYN-ACK on. No window-update ACK: the allowance equals the SYN-ACK window.
// - Send MSS 536: remote_mss keeps DEFAULT_MSS 536 when the SYN has no MSS option (558,
//   611, 1905-1913); with no TS the effective MSS is min(1460, 536) (2313-2320, 2630-2632).
// - The 1000-byte echo fits the 65535-byte peer window and Cubic's 1 MiB
//   initial window. MSS 536 splits it into 536 and 464 bytes, both at once.
//   No Nagle hold delays the tail; PSH marks the segment emptying the TX buffer.
// - Close as in echo-and-close.pkt (RFC 9293 FIN close).

0     < S 0:0(0) win 65535
+0    > S. 0:0(0) ack 1 win 48240 <mss 1460>
+0    < . 1:1(0) ack 1 win 65535
+0    < P. 1:1001(1000) ack 1 win 65535
+0    > . 1:537(536) ack 1001 win 48240
+0    > P. 537:1001(464) ack 1001 win 48240
+0    < . 1001:1001(0) ack 1001 win 65535
+0    < F. 1001:1001(0) ack 1001 win 65535
+0    > . 1001:1001(0) ack 1002 win 48240
+0    > F. 1001:1001(0) ack 1002 win 48240
+0    < . 1002:1002(0) ack 1002 win 65535
